        <p>- SATino 21sT AVGI3i*T,, BRIDGE FOOT</p>
        <p>116NIiE111, SANKEY, AND DISTRICT GARDEN AND CAGE BIRD SOCIETY. ANNUAL SHOW ON 14th AUGUST, 1915. Open at 3 o'dlock. PENKETH TANNERY PRIZE BAND. 'PTS of FLOWERS, FRUIT and VEGETABLES are invAed for the Belgian Famine Fund. EEPItESTAIENTS, SPORTS, COMPETITIONS, etc., in charge of the Local Belgian Relief Committee. ankeY (Cheshire Lines), Fiddler's Ferry (L. and N.-W.), and Sankey Tram. ADMISSION 6d.</p>
        <p>LATCHFORD GARDEN SOCIETY. President: The Rev. G. C. BRIG-GS, M.A. THE THIRD ANNUAL. FLOWER SHOW</p>
        <p>Will be held THIS DAY (SATURDAY), AUGUST 14th, In WASH-LANE SCHOOLS and PARK adjoining. OPENING CEREMONY by His Worship the MAYOR and the MAYORESS, at 3 p.m. SELECTIONS and ENTERTAINMENTS by the LATCHFORD ORCHESTRAL and ENTERTAINING SOCIETY. NOVEL COMPETITIONS in aid of Wounded Soldiers at Raddon Court Military Hospital. REFRESHMENTS at Reasonable Prices: ADMISSION. gd.- A ').//1., GEO. HOOPER, 1 Joint J. S. BURGEbB. I Hon. beCS.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CITIZENS' TEMPERANCE LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>PLEDGE SIGNING CAMPAIGN. SONS OF TEMPERANCE NIGHT. 'OPEN-AIR MEETING, FRIDAY NEXT, AITGIIST 20, BEWSEY-STREET, 7.30 p.m. SPeaker: Bro. R. MoINT.YRE (N.D. Organiser),</p>
        <p>ofillanchester. Bro. W. BURROWS, G.W.P.' of St. Helens, will Preside. Come and Sign the King's Pledge. I Temperance Workers, Please Rally!</p>
        <p>WHITE HEATHER DA+,</p>
        <p>SATURDAY NEXT, AUGUST 21st,</p>
        <p>IN AID OF 1,1)(' 1L CHARITIES.</p>
        <p>FETE IN THE ARPLEY CRICKET FIELD</p>
        <p>To be opened at 2.30 by MRS. HENRY GREENALL:</p>
        <p>ADMISSION, 2d. each. J. L. DAVENPORT, Chairman. J, TENNANT, 1 joint W. PATRICK, J Hon. Secs.</p>
        <p>Ladies interested in Local Charities are kindly Zquested .to attend a MEETING at the INFIRM- on TUESDAY EVENING NEXT, the 17th inßt • •, at 7.30.</p>
        <p>WORKING MEN'S INFIRMARY COMMITTEE. lu of the Warrington infirmary and the Fund Providing Comforts for the Soldiers and Sailors , operating at tin Dardanelles. 11.-MCIAL rEgTIVAL, BANK PARK, by ,kind permission of Ills Worship the Mayor and Corporation, SUNDAY, AUGUST 22nd, at 3 p.m. Grand Performance of Handel's Oratorio,</p>
        <p>"THE MESSIAL'?- 134;111g the combined Choirs honing denominationa,num eo toing 250, voices, and an efficient .Orchestra, tnnosed of local instiumeritalists. Leader of ,3010r,1114estra: Mr. T. Bradford, Barton, ,L.R.Alf.' Meidames SARA SILCOCK, JENNIE la_eigrn,RONG, E. A. SANDERS: Misses ELSIE laoo-4,..T, MAY HOCKENHALL: Messrs. W. Wll T. GOOSTREY E. PEARCE and • . RIGBY. OrC"duetor: Mr. H. PAYTON. Mus.Bac. Isfog,,an,ist: Mr. Henry L. Read. Ifus.Bac., F.R.C.O. A '-'n4rge for Admission. Collection at the Gates. 14inited number of seats, for which a small Payment will be expected.</p>
        <p>AT THE HIPPODROME 841tindly lent by Mr. Frank Macnaghten), `.11413AY EVENING, AUGUST 22nd, at 8,15, )13' GRAND CONCERT, iby the 13, AND of the 2nd BATT. S. lANCS. EGT., 'ind Permission of Colonel S. A. Moggridge• Conductor: Mr. R. E. CAHILL. vocaliets: Madame SARA SILCOCK and II • Mr. W. H. RIGBY. lices of Admission: is., 6d 4d., and 2nd. THOMAS BURTON. Chuirman. GEORGE WALKER, Vice-Chairman. J. H. J. HAMPSON, Hon. Secretary.</p>
        <p>tnbined Rehearsal of Orchestra and Chorus at 4. 1.0-street School on Tuesday next, the 17th gustl at 7.45 pan.</p>
        <p>OC AL NDS. THE WARRINGTON INFIRMARY. THE LOCAL RED CROSS FUNDS AT RADDON COURT, THELWALL, AND THE OAKLANDS. THE' LOCAL TOBACCO FUND. TO PROVIDE GIFTS FOR WOUNDED</p>
        <p>soLiii-Efiglic-Wif WARRINGTON DISTRICT, SALE BY AUCTION. _ _ _ _ _</p>
        <p>His Worship the Mayor (Alderman Peter Peacock), chairman of the Executive Committee, on their behalf, begs to remind the Public that the PARR HALL is NOW OPEN between the hours of 10 a.m. and 4 p.m. to receive their GIFTS to the above funds in the shape of , Furniture, Pictures, Curios, Useful and Ornamental Articles, or any- thing that could be sold by auction and converted into cash; of which there is imperative need.</p>
        <p>Most ICe:o;fe have articles laid aside for which they have no use; some have articles of value they could well spare.</p>
        <p>A direct appeal is made to all persons to contribute.</p>
        <p>It is requested that the donor will attach name and address, with a description of the article given, and a receipt will be returned. If it is inconvenient to send goods they will be called for on a request being sent to the Hon. Secre- tary, Rev. Irvine Lister, Town Hall.</p>
        <p>CIOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. NATIONAL REGISTRATION ACT, 1915. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Registration required by the above Act of all persons (male and female), between the ages of 15 and 65 (subject to certain exceptions), will be made on Sunday, the 15th day of August, 1915. Attention is called to the folle':ing instruc- tions .</p>
        <p>Every person between the ages stattd above must fill up a separate form. , The form must be filled up and signed on gn-• Jay.. 15th j%iigut..rr nts 4- " 19:12S;d'kt40041.7Spir' -tifricl leaves the cwn before Sunday„the 15th, he must take the form with Jim, fill up and sign it on. the Sunday and deliver it on the folloliing day to an Enumerator • in the district where he is staying. 'lf a person has not received a form on cr before Sunday, the 15th, he must, whether re- siding at home or temporarily absent in some other place, obtain a form on one of the three days 'following the Sunday, and must fill up, sign and deliver it at one of the places appointed by the Local Authority of the. District.</p>
        <p>-Persons are re-citie-s-t-jed—tO fill up the form in ink, and not to crease or fold it, and therefore not to use envelopes, as the Enumerators are compelled to open them immediately. The EnuMerators are bound to secrecy under heavy penalties.</p>
        <p>- Every assistance will be rendered by the Staff of the Local Registration Authority and by the duly appointed Enumerators, but it -vould ne convenient if 'applications for assistance or advice were made at the Central Office it tl,e Gymnasium, Palmyra-square. The Central Office will be open from 9 a.m. till 8 p.m. daily. j. LYON WHITTLE, ' Town Clerk. -- WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL. NATIONAL REGISTRATION ACT, 1915. NATIONAL REGISTRATION. IMPORTANT NOTICE. DUTY TO REGISTER. 1. Every person between the ages of 15 and 65 (with certain exceptions) is required to fill up and sign i a form of registration stating name; place of residence; age; and certain other par- ticulars.</p>
        <p>A form of registration to be 'filled up and sigfied will be left at the place of residence of each person before Sunday, the 15th of August, 1915.</p>
        <p>--PLACES WHERE NEW FORMS MAY BE OBTAINED. 2. Any person between the ages of 15 and 65 who may not before Sunday, the 15th of August, 1915, have received a form of registration, or who quay have lost, or destrolyed, or spoilt it, or who has otherwise been prevented from filling up the form on or before Sunday, the 15th of , . August, 1915,may obtain a form by applying at ANY POST OFFICE WITHIN THE WAR- RINGTON RURAL DISTRICT, on the 16th, 17th, and 18th of August. 1915. Also at the fol- lowing Post Offices: Folly-lane, Padgate-lane, Sankey Bridges. ATTENDANCE BEFORE LOCAL REGISTRA-</p>
        <p>TION AUTHORITY. 3. If a person, liable to fill up and sign a form of registration has not done so, or if the form which he or she, has filled up, signed and returned, is incomplete or incorrect, the Local Registration Authority may require such per- son to attend before them to answer such ques- tions as may be necessary to enable such form to be filled up properly. CHANGE OF ADDRESS. 4. If any person registered under the above Act changes his or her place of residence and has come‘to reside within this area, he or she shall, unless such change is merely temporary, within trenty-eight days thereafter send or deliver to the Local Registration Authority of this area at the address given below by post or otherwise, his or her certificate of registration with the new place of residence noted thereon. Such person shall thereupon he entitled to be flpplied with a fresh certificate of registration. NEW ARRIVALS IN THE UNITED KINGDOM TO REGISTER.</p>
        <p>5. Witl-Ciii-.Tw—enty---eigla days after the arrival in the United Kingdom of any person between the ages of 15 and 65 he or she shall, if not previously registered, and if residing in this area, send or deliver to the Local Registra- tion Authority of this area by post or other- wise, notice d his or her arrival, together with particulars concerning himself or herself re- quired by the above-mentioned Aet to be regis- tered. He or she shall, if so required, attend at such place and time as the Authority may appoint and shall answer such questions as may be addressed to him or her for the purpose of enabling the necessary particulars to be regis- tered, and thereupon shall be supplied with a certificate of registration. A form of registra- tion to be filled up and signed may be obtained by such person from the undersigned.</p>
        <p>PENALTIES. 6. Refusal. or neglect to observe the above provisions is, in the case of a person over eighteen years of age required to register ,him- self or herself, an offence for which the party offending is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding £5, and in the case of a continuing offence to a further fine not exceeding ..t1 for each day during which the offence pontinues (5 and 6, Geo. 5, c. 60, s. 13 (3)). C. suTTON, Clerk. Bewsey Chambers. Warrington, 3rd August, 1915.</p>
