      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0076" n="art0076">
        <head>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</head>
        <p>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</p>
        <p>--Notices of births. marriages, and deaths, in, memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in "The Examiner" at the following rates :—Not .exceeding 20 words, is. 6d. each; every additional seven .worda. 6d.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0077" n="art0077">
        <head>Marriages.</head>
        <p>Marriages.</p>
        <p>DUNABIN—BEILL.—On the 9th inst.. at Penketh Wesleyan Church. by the Rev. E. ff. GaWllO, John, son of Mr. and Mrs. T. Dunabin. of Hope House. Penketh, to ,Annie, daughter of the late Mr. T. and Mrs. Bell, of Burmholni,••Chopel-road, Pen- ketia. - - - -</p>
        <p>---- SLAYER--EVANS.—On the 31st ult., at Orford Church. by the Rev. G. Vale Owen. Albert. son of William Mayer, of 80, Orford-avenue, to Alice, daughter of Williams Evans, of 50, Chester-road. TUCKER--OXLET.---On the 9th inst.. at Penketh Wesleyan Chapel. by the Rev. H. T. Dixon, William Pic:Acton Tucker, fifth son of Mr. and Mrs. 10/111 Tucker, of Victoria-terrace, Penketh. to Miss Ethel Oxley. daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Oxley, of -Station-road. Penketh.</p>
        <p>;TV</p>
        <p>Deaths. • .-,BEIaNEY.--Angtigt eth, at 173,-Bevisey-road, Alice Martha Agatha Berney. aged 58 years. 0"' ' • - ".124arr . —Alum st 9th, at 57; Weet-etreet."Marr Clayton, aged -56 Years. -OLEAVE.—Augast 10th, at 10, Buckley-street, aoseph Gleame, aged 68 yea-re.</p>
        <p>YATES.—Auraet 19th, at 19, Eldon-street. Annie .7ates, aged 21) years.</p>
