        <p>tit NEI ~ TALKS. , .., ~ , . _ ciWhilst it is dearly the duty of the Government to bring home I.) the community the facts concerning the value of money during the present crisis, it is equally important that the community should take notice of the Government's instructions. .q The splendid response .to the War Loan is evidence of the people's desire to* help. There are thousands, however, who are making more wages at the present time than they ever made before, or are likely to make in the future, and who have not yet realized the necessity for saving. If each worker will set aside his extra earnings and deposit them in the Savings Bank, he will not only be helping to provide "silver bullets" to beat the Germans, but he will be making it easier, for himself, his wife and children to overcome the slump in trade when the war is over. _ , 1 1 If you have a Savings Bank Account, and know tlfat you can i withdraw a little money. when It is needed, it will make your life happier and give you an independence which a person in debt never has, or can ever hope to have. It is quite true that money "talks." . ..._ AT YOUR SE]R.VirCal : f The 'WErrillgton, Runcorn &amp; District 17 71 k T Sl4 iir iIN OS it 0. ANK. ESTABLISHED 1818. Head Office BLTIERMARKET-STREET. Branches ' BANK QUAY, 29, GREEN-STREET. , EARLESTOWN, 5, QUEEN-STREET. Runcorn Office 10, HIGH-STREET. '</p>
