        <p>WOUNDED. FIGHTING THE TURKS. Crosileld's .Men Wounded In The Dardanelles. News has reached 'Mrs. Crooks, of 18, Bewsey- road, that her son, Albert William, who was orikinally a first-class stoker on board one of His MajestY's battleships, but who is now fighting with the Royal Naval Reservists in the vicinity of the Dardanelles, is in hospital suffering from an ulcer in his eye. Writing from the Royal Naval Hospital, Valetta, Malta, he says : " I expect that I will be going back into the trenches to put out a few more Turks in another</p>
