        <p>WAR OFFICE AND MISSING SOLDIERS, New Scheme. The Press Bureau issued tie feilowiag on Thursday night The War Office has arranged to issue to the Inquiry Department of the Red Cross, Norfolk Nouse, St. James'-square, LAlWart, official copies of lists of missing 'officers and me*, and, so far as possible, to grant facilities to depart- ments aid agents to make iequivies among the wounded as regards all men on the missing list. If such inquiries result in- establishing that the missing officer or man is a prisoner of war or has died, the result will bo reported to the War Office, who will take 'the matter up, offi- cially notifying the next-of-kin, &amp;e. All in- quiries as regards tine' issiig, aalireased to Red Cross Inquiry Department, will, however, also be answered direct, 411111 all reliable infor- mation received will be communicated. Inquirers should give name, Christian name, regimental number, regiment, battalion, com- pany or platoon, and the slate of casualty. For the Royal Artillery the battery is necessary, and for the Royal Engineers and Army Service I Corps the company.</p>
